          "tarball_url": "https://github.com/Mosaad-M/tls/archive/refs/tags/v1.4.1.tar.gz",
          "sha256": "f7bdfb019707dffa34a44316eeae3fb1f0c3f9199d42ca5b4eafc791c5a34c28",
          "mojo_requires": ">=1.0.0",
          "deps": [],
          "changelog": "Fix load_system_ca_bundle passing a non-NUL-terminated path to open() (failed on Linux)"
        },
        {
          "version": "1.4.2",
          "published_at": "2026-10-01",
          "tarball_url": "https://github.com/Mosaad-M/tls/archive/refs/tags/v1.4.2.tar.gz",
          "sha256": "ff36cd90175f9f9763313dc0dc43ff39f257c3ee3fc039bb1e36c177b1338075",
          "mojo_requires": ">=1.0.0",
          "deps": [],
          "changelog": "Accept certificate chains anchored at a cross-signed root (fixes HTTPS on Linux for e.g. Google Trust Services chains); exact byte comparison for keys"
        },
        {
          "version": "1.4.3",
          "published_at": "2026-10-03",
          "tarball_url": "https://github.com/Mosaad-M/tls/archive/refs/tags/v1.4.3.tar.gz",
          "sha256": "7a702e1998c4a44e7f111306d64f8ba1dd903780d3e26113453a7b1346cefb57",
          "mojo_requires": ">=1.0.0",
          "deps": [],
          "changelog": "SECURITY (critical): certificate path validation now enforces CA constraints (basicConstraints, keyUsage, EKU, pathLen, name chaining, critical extensions); earlier versions let any trusted leaf certificate impersonate any host. Validity times fail closed."
        },
        {
          "version": "1.4.4",
          "published_at": "2026-10-05",
          "tarball_url": "https://github.com/Mosaad-M/tls/archive/refs/tags/v1.4.4.tar.gz",
          "sha256": "59589db20f78741e9684eada044128fcb1939111ae284e9e1db2c0d7c93f8d7e",
          "mojo_requires": ">=1.0.0",
          "deps": [],
          "changelog": "SECURITY: recv_all() requires an authenticated close_notify (truncation; allow_truncation=True opts out); plaintext/undecryptable post-handshake alerts rejected; RSA PKCS#1 out-of-bounds read fixed; all-zero X25519 secret rejected; TLS 1.3 downgrade sentinel checked; TLS 1.3 padding stripped; no PKCS#1 in TLS 1.3 CertificateVerify; *.com wildcards rejected. Interop: RSA-PSS in TLS 1.2 ServerKeyExchange."
        },
        {
          "version": "1.4.5",
          "published_at": "2026-10-05",
          "tarball_url": "https://github.com/Mosaad-M/tls/archive/refs/tags/v1.4.5.tar.gz",
          "sha256": "10f2f472e5224845ba53771cb046765224b18cde2c604ab9d4530f3dd7e3864c",
          "mojo_requires": ">=1.0.0",
          "deps": [],
          "changelog": "TLS 1.3 KeyUpdate (server key rotation no longer breaks connections; update requests answered). Socket I/O: resumable read timeouts reported as 'tls: read timed out', no SIGPIPE on writes to closed peers, EINTR retried, TlsSocket.set_timeout()."
        },
        {
          "version": "1.4.6",
          "published_at": "2026-10-05",
          "tarball_url": "https://github.com/Mosaad-M/tls/archive/refs/tags/v1.4.6.tar.gz",
          "sha256": "4b00407e0f8d310edc92f1d3189af0fc2779620c681e39c83d3e60cdb8f63c8f",
          "mojo_requires": ">=1.0.0",
          "deps": [],
          "changelog": "SECURITY: constant-time AES (bitsliced), GHASH (table-free) and P-256 secret-key operations (key generation, ECDH, ECDSA signing); removes cache-timing and scalar-length timing leaks. AES-GCM ~8x and P-256 ~3x faster."
        },
        {
          "version": "1.5.0",
          "published_at": "2026-10-05",
          "tarball_url": "https://github.com/Mosaad-M/tls/archive/refs/tags/v1.5.0.tar.gz",
          "sha256": "dd60774534b48c5c056ce2d23465cd9e0d7995e33888412bc2eea79223229cbd",
          "mojo_requires": ">=1.0.0",
          "deps": [],
          "changelog": "TLS 1.3 HelloRetryRequest (P-256/P-384); TLS 1.2 extended master secret and renegotiation_info; constant-time P-384 key exchange. Fixes: TLS 1.2 SHA-384 suites used the SHA-256 PRF; servers with P-384 ECDSA certificates could not connect."
        },
        {
          "version": "1.6.0",
          "published_at": "2026-10-06",
          "tarball_url": "https://github.com/Mosaad-M/tls/archive/refs/tags/v1.6.0.tar.gz",
          "sha256": "35d4ab19d9ecfb9ba78d4dbf2e19280e5ce8a7af212b7e6c3bfc48293758b237",
          "mojo_requires": ">=1.0.0",
          "deps": [],
          "changelog": "SECURITY: fixes from a second review. A malformed certificate crashed the process; unbounded handshake buffering before authentication; strict TLS 1.2/1.3 state machines (also fixes servers that fragment handshake messages, e.g. facebook.com); nameConstraints and intermediate EKU enforced; RSA >= 2048; strict protocol/DER/signature parsing; TLS 1.2 mTLS over SHA-384 suites fixed."
        },
        {
          "version": "1.6.1",
          "published_at": "2026-10-07",
          "tarball_url": "https://github.com/Mosaad-M/tls/archive/refs/tags/v1.6.1.tar.gz",
          "sha256": "680928daec20944d891dca7c2fbf0ab02dc2c20a7a10edd9525a1cb7c441b662",
          "mojo_requires": ">=1.0.0",
          "deps": [],
          "changelog": "SHA-512 signatures (RSA PKCS#1/PSS, ecdsa-with-SHA512 and RSA-PSS SHA-512 certificates, TLS 1.3/1.2 rsa_pss_rsae_sha512 and TLS 1.2 rsa_pkcs1_sha512); AES-GCM keys prepared once per connection (64-byte records 4.9 -> 2.9 us); every peer-facing parser fuzzed in CI."
        },
        {
          "version": "1.7.0",
          "published_at": "2026-10-07",
          "tarball_url": "https://github.com/Mosaad-M/tls/archive/refs/tags/v1.7.0.tar.gz",
          "sha256": "ed14f36d2d39a37d7625e1d4f01c5aac916d09b942a69daf98e67b908ca2048d",
          "mojo_requires": ">=1.0.0",
          "deps": [],
          "changelog": "Works alongside Mojo's std: declares no C function std declares (open/read/write, errno), so programs using tls with open(), listdir or get_errno compile again. Sockets use recv/send everywhere; CA bundles over 2 MB are no longer cut off. websocket <= 1.1.3 clashes with it: use websocket >= 1.2.0."
        }
      ]
    },
